{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_arzjgn75guvf76237i65megd63apv2z3xafl2nzrtpkn7tqaxz5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single 967-line C file: a trimmed copy of **stb_ds** (Sean Barrett's dynamic array / hash map library) plus the `strkey` / `str_put` helpers from its test section. The public header only declares `str_put`, but the build globs the whole file, so the real ABI is the 16 symbols below.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` (1262 lines) — full translation, all exports `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`\n\n## Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n`nm -D` on the C `.so` vs the Rust `.so` → **identical 16-symbol sets**:\n`stbds_arrgrowf, stbds_arrfreef, stbds_rand_seed, stbds_hash_string, stbds_hash_bytes, stbds_hmget_key, stbds_hmget_key_ts, stbds_hmput_default, stbds_hmput_key, stbds_hmdel_key, stbds_hmfree_func, stbds_shmode_func, stbds_stralloc, stbds_strreset, strkey, str_put`\n\n## Faithfully reproduced C quirks (bugs kept, not fixed)\n- **SipHash sign-extension UB**: `d[3] << 24` is `int` arithmetic that goes negative and sign-extends into `size_t`, corrupting the high word. Translated as `i32 → i64 → usize`, so hashes match bit-for-bit (tested with 0x80/0xff byte patterns).\n- **`printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)`** passes a whole 16-byte struct for `%s`; per SysV AMD64 it lands in two INTEGER registers, so `%s` eats `key` and `%d` eats `value`. Output is `a <num>` — confirmed against the C `.so` and reproduced by calling libc `printf` with the equivalent register contents.\n- **Missing `temp_key` update** in the wrap-around branch of `stbds_hmput_key` (present only in the first probe loop) — left asymmetric; it reproduces the same stale-pointer/double-free abort as C, with identical exit code 134 and identical stderr.\n- `stbds_arrgrowf(NULL, e, 0, 0)` returning `NULL`, `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` computing an invalid pointer, wrapping multiplies, `hash_seed * a + b` LCG constants derived through the original `load_32_or_64` macro steps.\n- Same allocator (libc `realloc`/`free`) and same stdio `FILE`, so memory and buffering interop with C.\n- `const _: () =` layout asserts pin the structs to C sizes (32/16/24/128/104 bytes).\n\n## Differential verification (my own, not self-reported)\nA `dlopen` driver exercising every exported symbol — array growth, all 5 hash seeds × 4 byte patterns × lengths 0–41, string hashing, binary/wide-key maps with 300 inserts + deletes + tombstone reuse + shrink/rehash, string maps in DEFAULT/STRDUP/ARENA modes, arena block growth, `strkey`, and `str_put` for 7 inputs:\n\n- **6887 lines of output: `cmp` byte-identical** (C vs Rust)\n- **60 randomized fuzz rounds** (900 mixed ops each): identical stdout, stderr, and exit codes\n- Repeated against the **assert-enabled C build** (no `-DNDEBUG`): also byte-identical\n- `c_src/` confirmed unmodified (`diff -r` against a pre-work copy)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":108427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1384,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14c661ae-ae47-42f0-b327-43df9bce8539","uuid":"cdc1b84c-92df-4bcf-b646-5dbb93cff916","timestamp":"2026-08-20T05:14:31.845Z"}
